            <div xml:id="d723">

                <pb facs="1203" n="1189" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62114 Sick/12–2344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Huddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-23T15:00:00+01:00">December 23,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 24—3:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8293. American Interests, Germany, Civilian Exchange. Following is substance
                    Swiss note dated December 22:</p>
                <p>Foreign Office transmitted to Swiss Legation Berlin communications based on
                    Madrid’s 3708, November 9 to Department<anchor n="63" xml:id="d723-f1"/> and
                    Department’s 3928, November 18.</p>
                <pb facs="1204" n="1190" xml:id="pg1190"/>
                <p>Swiss Legation states with regard Switzerland’s right to take steps include
                    Paraguayans in forthcoming exchange that Germany never contested American
                    Government’s right to make exchange proposals in name of all western hemisphere
                    countries. German Foreign Office never objected to Swiss Government conducting
                    exchange negotiations on behalf of countries not represented by Switzerland.
                    However Swiss Legation thus far only proposed to Germans for exchange nationals
                    of Swiss protected countries, this likewise applicable to from 50 to 57 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">75</hi>] bearers of Latin American documentation to be
                    exchanged in Category F. Swiss Legation nevertheless informed Germans that
                    American Government envisages special German-Paraguayan and German-Colombian
                    exchanges (Department’s 3928, November 18 and Legation’s 7684, November 22).</p>
                <p>Concerning Paraguay, Swiss Legation has Spanish Embassy’s consent to designate
                    for exchange certain of bearers Paraguayan documents at Bergen-Belsen. It
                    accordingly appears that Switzerland’s right to act for Paraguayans in
                    organizing general American-German exchange is settled with Spanish
                    representative and German Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>[Here follow data on lists of exchange candidates.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
